      text: AES 256 Replacement Using OpenSSL Data encryption is being migrated to AES 256 encryption leveraging OpenSSL. This change applies to data stored in the Siebel Database, the Siebel Gateway Registry, and Siebel Server services. NOTE: Customerswillrequire at least some minimal downtime for this encryption replacement. This applies to this Monthly Update (25.10), but if, for example, a customer is later updating from 24.9 to 25.12, the downtime required for this change will occur at that time. For more information on this, please see the following documentation: • For customers on traditional Siebel CRM architectures, please review My Oracle Support Alert_Special_ _Considerations for Updating Siebel from pre-25.10 to_ _25.10 or Later_ (Doc ID 3107936.1) • For customers who are on a Siebel CRM container deployment, please additionally review My Oracle Support Alert_Special Considerations for Updating Siebel_ _from pre-25.10 to 25.10 or Later When Running on_ _Containers_(Doc ID 3107887.1) Training on this feature is available onOracle University. • Security Guide • Install Guide No
