      text: Category Migration Subcategory Synchronous Bug No 37937312 Data migrations can be synchronous or asynchronous. Those customers using Application Deployment Manager (ADM) as part of their migrations will find that synchronous migrations fail due to generated cookies that are incompatible with Tomcat 10.1 which rejects them. In 25.6 we updated Tomcat to version 10.1 since we have updated Java to Java 21 and must update the way cookies are generated during synchronous migrations. The previous version of Tomcat (9) allowed cookie headers to have commas “,” in them and now requires semicolons “;” instead.
